WEBVTT

00:14.400 --> 00:18.801
Anthropic's playbook for delivering
software with agents has six stages.

00:18.901 --> 00:23.566
Plan, design, build, test, deploy,
maintain.

00:23.666 --> 00:25.551
Agents now run all six.

00:25.651 --> 00:28.016
So code is no longer the bottleneck.

00:28.566 --> 00:29.655
So what is?

00:29.755 --> 00:31.533
Knowing what correct means.

00:31.633 --> 00:36.048
Agents build from written plans and specs,
so that has to come first.

00:36.498 --> 00:37.783
Code got cheap.

00:37.883 --> 00:39.538
Correct got valuable.

00:41.288 --> 00:43.552
And agents even write their own tests.

00:43.652 --> 00:45.761
Here's one, from lab one.

00:45.861 --> 00:48.806
The spec promises a discount on bigger
orders.

00:48.906 --> 00:52.746
The agent's test copied the app's total,
with no discount.

00:52.846 --> 00:55.209
The agent tested what the app does.

00:55.309 --> 00:56.967
You test what it should do.

00:57.067 --> 00:58.568
That's your first find.

01:00.418 --> 01:01.842
Testing by hand today?

01:01.942 --> 01:03.318
You already do this.

01:03.418 --> 01:05.962
You read the rules, and you spot what's
off.

01:06.712 --> 01:07.746
What grows?

01:07.846 --> 01:11.319
Writing down what correct means, before
agents build.

01:11.419 --> 01:13.596
Reviewing the evidence they bring back.

01:13.696 --> 01:15.223
Deciding what ships.

01:15.323 --> 01:16.924
Fixing selectors all day?

01:17.024 --> 01:18.310
Nobody will miss that.

01:18.410 --> 01:20.085
That's leading the agents.

01:20.185 --> 01:22.625
Hands-on work, not a job title.

01:23.075 --> 01:25.570
Most teams are trying AI in testing.

01:25.670 --> 01:27.195
Few have it working yet.

01:27.295 --> 01:29.024
That gap needs testers.

01:29.774 --> 01:32.176
So we built a free path to get you ready.

01:32.276 --> 01:37.598
Each tutorial: a short video, a lab in
your browser, an automatic check, and a

01:37.638 --> 01:39.072
free certificate.

01:39.172 --> 01:41.040
Everyone starts with lab one.

01:41.140 --> 01:42.329
Never written code?

01:42.429 --> 01:43.347
That's fine.

01:43.387 --> 01:45.601
We'll shape and improve the path as we
learn.

01:46.351 --> 01:47.635
Code got cheap.

01:47.735 --> 01:49.390
Correct got valuable.

01:49.490 --> 01:51.952
Open lab one and make your first find.

01:52.052 --> 01:54.126
Get ready to lead the agents.
